1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,830
This tunnel was reportedly built so patients wouldn't see the dead leave.

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:05,290
Waverly Hills, Kentucky.

3
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:07,180
A tuberculosis hospital.

4
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:09,050
Opened in 1910.

5
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:12,480
By 1926, five storeys stood on the hill.

6
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,700
And about five hundred feet of concrete tunnel ran down it.

7
00:00:16,030 --> 00:00:18,910
So many died that staff, it's said, moved the bodies out of

8
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:19,930
sight, for morale.

9
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:24,600
It closed in 1961, after antibiotics beat back the disease.

10
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:26,650
But visitors say something stayed.

11
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:28,850
Shadow figures on the fourth floor.

12
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:31,230
A little boy who rolls a ball back.

13
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:34,290
Legend says sixty-three thousand people died here.

14
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:37,670
Historians estimate closer to six to eight thousand.

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,700
Sceptics note the building now sells ghost tours.

16
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:42,770
And long concrete halls echo.

17
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:45,170
So who sends the ball back?

18
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,750
Ask anyone at Waverly, and they'll tell you:
